# The seed knows none of `__Raw.osDebugHost`, `__Raw.dbgEnvironmentValue`, `__Raw.dbgAttachSegment`,
# `__Raw.dbgCtlAddr`, `__Raw.dbgTextBase`, `__Raw.dbgTextLimit`, `__Raw.dbgServiceEntryAddr`,
# `__Raw.osThreadCreate`, `__Raw.schedTlsTebOffsetAddr`, `__Raw.schedAllMachinesAddr` or
# `__Raw.schedPreemptExtLockAddr`, so it refuses `runtime/DebugAgent.maxon` at the first call to one
# (E3004). Every table that TEACHES those rows — `RawIntrinsics`, `StdDialect`, the x64 lowering, the
# `IatSlot` band, `TargetFacilities` — is left standing, so `C1` knows them and compiles the unshimmed
# tree into `C2`.
#
# The tier file keeps every constant `checkDebugAgentGeometry` pins and every entry point the roots name;
# only the eleven rows are swapped for rows the seed already has, which makes each body inert rather than
# absent. The second hunk turns the agent OFF in the shimmed build, because an inert agent that the entry
# stub still called would attach to whatever the substituted rows answered.
